# Ragtop's repository is the plugin: everything here is cloned onto a user's
# machine by `omarchy plugin add`, and everything here is read by whoever
# decides whether to trust it. So this file is less about tidiness than about
# keeping things out that were never meant to ship.

# Anything an assistant or editor leaves behind. None of it is part of the
# plugin, and some of it is a transcript of someone's working day.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.cursor/
.aider*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Python, which the helpers are written in. Generated bytecode is noise on a
# machine that byte-compiles on first run anyway.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Working copies and archives. A .bak next to the file it backs up is how a
# half-finished edit gets published.
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
*.zip

# Ragtop's own runtime state belongs in ~/.local/state/ragtop and
# $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, never here; these are the names it would use if something
# were ever run from inside the checkout.
protocol-bindings/
install.conf
settings.conf
.ragtop-base
